.\" Man page for the Sleela compiler and runtime front end.
.\" Kept in lockstep with impl/frontend/driver.cpp usage; the binary is the
.\" authority. Build the binary with: cd impl && make build/sleela
.TH SLEELA 1 "2026-10-29" "SLeeLa 0.3.30-dev" "SLeeLa Manual"
.SH NAME
sleela \- SLeeLa compiler and runtime front end (Sleelvac(TM))
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sleela
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sleela
is the authoritative SLeeLa compiler and runtime, also known as
Sleelvac(TM). It parses, resolves referenced library units, checks semantics,
compiles
.I .sleela
source into a runnable Core artifact, and executes artifacts and supported
source/framework input on the native C/C++ Core VM. The supported source-syntax
range is 1.0 \(en 2.8 (see
.BR sleela-syntax (7)
and the in-tree
.IR SLEELA.syntax ).
.PP
A SLeeLa program is a
.IR .sleela
source file (a "Wrapper(TM)"). The companion
.B nordshrift
tool performs the Nordshrift round-trip; it is documented separately.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These appear
.I before
the command.
.TP
.BR \-\-memory\-manager ", " \-\-mm
Enable the Memory Manager with the default 2 GiB limit.
.TP
.BI \-\-memory\-manager= SIZE ", " \-\-mm= SIZE
Enable the Memory Manager with a byte limit;
.BR K ", " M ", and " G
suffixes are accepted.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Source and artifact commands
.TP
.B sleela compile \fR[\fIglobal-options\fR] \fIfile.sleela\fR [\fImore.sleela\fR ...] \fB\-o\fR \fIoutput.sleela\fR
Compile one or more source files to a runnable Core artifact.
.TP
.B sleela check \fIfile.sleela\fR
Parse, resolve referenced library units, and check semantics. Exits non-zero on
any error; this is the fail-closed validation gate.
.TP
.B sleela run \fIfile\fR [\fImore-files\fR ...]
Run a Core artifact, or run supported source/framework input directly. Accepted
inputs:
.IR .sleela ", " .xclass ", " .java ", " .kt ", " .scala ", " .groovy ", and " .clj .
.TP
.B sleela validate\-artifact \fIfile.sleela\fR
Validate the runnable artifact ABI and format.
.TP
.B sleela version
Print the compiler/runtime version string.
.SS Other commands
.TP
.B sleela http\-server \fR<1|2|3> [\fB\-\-port\fR N] [\fB\-\-threads\fR N] [\fB\-\-root\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-log\fR FILE] [\fB\-\-once\fR]
Serve over HTTP/1, HTTP/2, or HTTP/3.
.TP
.B sleela xclass \fR[\fB\-\-run\fR|\fB\-\-emit\fR|\fB\-\-info\fR] \fIfile.xclass\fR [...]
Operate on compiled-class input (default
.BR \-\-run ).
.TP
.B sleela langin \fR[\fB\-\-run\fR|\fB\-\-emit\-sleela\fR|\fB\-\-emit\-xclass\fR|\fB\-\-info\fR] \fIfile.java\fR|\fI.kt\fR|\fI.scala\fR|\fI.groovy\fR|\fI.clj\fR [...]
Bring JVM-family source into SLeeLa (default
.BR \-\-run ;
.B \-\-emit
aliases
.BR \-\-emit\-sleela ).
.TP
.B sleela nordshrift \fR[\fB\-\-emit\fR|\fB\-\-roundtrip\fR] [\fB\-\-target=\fRsleela|java|c] \fIfile.sleela\fR
Run the Nordshrift round-trip (default target
.BR sleela ).
.TP
.B sleela vm \fR[list|select <native|1..10|premium 1..11>|info <selection>|run <premium <1..11>|p<N>|native> <program>]
Select and run a SLeeLa Virtual Machine generation.
.TP
.B sleela modium \fR[scan [native|1..10] [\fB\-\-exact\fR] [\fB\-\-seal\fR]|status|restore <1..10>]
Module-integrity scanning and restore.
.TP
.B sleela registry \fR[review|get|set|feature|save|export]
Inspect and edit the runtime registry.
.TP
.B sleela native \fR[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-mm\fR[=\fIsize\fR]] [\fB\-\-\fR] \fIprogram\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
Run a program against the native configuration;
.B \-\-
ends option parsing.
.TP
.B sleela exec \fR[...]
As
.BR native ,
for executing a program.
.TP
.B sleela design\-activity \fIscience correctness reproducibility observability safety resource interoperability\fR
Report a design-activity score across the seven axes.
.TP
.B sleela defender \fR<detect|fetch|build|install|provision> [\fIdirectory\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-defender\fR|\fB\-\-optin\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-sha256\fR \fIhex\fR]
OS Defender provisioning.
.B detect
is read-only;
.BR fetch / build / install / provision
require
.B \-\-allow\-defender
or
.BR SLEELA_DEFENDER_OPTIN=1 .
.TP
.B sleela docs \fR[\fIpackage\fR] [\fIClassName\fR] | \fB\-\-generate\fR [\fIdir\fR] | \fB\-\-live\fR ... | \fB\-\-facade\fR \fItopic\fR [\fB\-\-facade\-root\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-facade\-max\-mb\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-facade\-max\-files\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-facade\-max\-seconds\fR \fIN\fR]
SleelaDoc in the terminal: the SLeeLa documentation brand, reachable from the
command line. With no arguments it lists every documentable topic (packages and
units). Given a
.I package
(e.g.
.BR crypto )
it prints that package and its units; given a
.I ClassName
(e.g.
.BR stringbuilder ,
resolved case-insensitively and by the SL\(hy prefix) it prints a rich page:
definition, design purpose, relationships, structure, user clays, and a mastery
ladder. A
.I package ClassName
pair selects the exact unit. An unknown topic yields ranked near ("did you
mean") results.
.IP
.B \-\-generate
.RI [ dir ]
writes the plain\(hytext doc corpus (default
.IR api/sleela/docs ):
one
.I <package>/<Unit>.txt
per class, a
.I <package>/_package.txt
overview, and a
.I TOPICS.index .
The CLI prefers a present corpus;
.B \-\-live
forces live parsing.
.IP
.B \-\-facade
.I topic
searches the filesystem at runtime for a facade topic's real folders and files
(folders first \(em the shape of the subject \(em then the files), rendering any
.I .sleela
sources as full pages. The search defaults to the SLeeLa root and is widened
with
.B \-\-facade\-root
(up to
.IR / )
or
.BR SLEELA_FACADE_PATH .
It is bounded by three user\(hyoverridable caps \(em
.B \-\-facade\-max\-mb
(default 6 MB),
.B \-\-facade\-max\-files
(default 6000), and
.B \-\-facade\-max\-seconds
(default 360, i.e. 6 minutes) \(em and always prints an honest partial report
naming whichever cap stopped it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SLEELA_SHA256_MANIFEST
Path to the trusted SHA-256 manifest. The build and execution gate verifies
every covered source file against this manifest and fails closed on a mismatch.
Regenerate it after editing covered sources with
.IR "python3 tools/generate-sha256-manifest.py \-\-root . \-\-output security/sha256-manifest.json" .
.TP
.B SLEELA_DEFENDER_OPTIN
When set to 1, authorizes the privileged
.B defender
subcommands.
.TP
.B SLEELA_DEFENDER_ALLOW_ROOT
When set to 1, explicitly authorizes privileged installation.
.TP
.B SLEELA_DOCS_DIR
Location of the pre-generated SleelaDoc text corpus that
.B sleela docs
prefers when present (default
.IR <root>/api/sleela/docs ).
.TP
.B SLEELA_FACADE_PATH
Default search root for
.BR "sleela docs \-\-facade" ,
overriding the SLeeLa root (the
.B \-\-facade\-root
option takes precedence over this).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B sleela
exits 0 on success and non-zero on a parse, resolution, semantic, verification,
or runtime error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Validate and run a standard-library demo:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sleela check lib/philosophers/philosophers-demo.sleela
sleela run   lib/philosophers/philosophers-demo.sleela
.EE
.RE
.PP
Compile two sources to a Core artifact, then validate it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sleela compile a.sleela b.sleela -o out.sleela
sleela validate-artifact out.sleela
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run with the Memory Manager capped at 512 MiB:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sleela --mm=512M run program.sleela
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I SLEELA.syntax
The normative language-syntax specification (syntax 1.0 \(en 2.8).
.TP
.I lib/LIBRARY.SYMBOLS.md
The authoritative /lib class vocabulary.
.TP
.I security/sha256-manifest.json
The trusted manifest consulted by the verification gate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nordshrift (1),
.BR sleela-syntax (7)
.PP
In-tree:
.IR SLEELA.syntax ", " README.md ", " "tutorial/README.md" ,
and the
